        "original_id": "54c01063-ab8e-531d-983d-f000a6b89958",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands and music acts: Daisy Chainsaw, Generationals, Queenadreena, Ruby Throat\n- People: KatieJane Garside, Ted Joyner, Grant Widmer\n- Places: England, New Orleans, Louisiana\n- Albums and releases: Eleventeen, Con Law, early EPs, Lullabies in a Glass Wilderness\n\nFacts:\n- Daisy Chainsaw were an English alternative rock band active from 1989 to 1995.\n- KatieJane Garside was Daisy Chainsaw's original lead vocalist and lyricist on the band's early EPs and debut album, \"Eleventeen\" (1992).\n- KatieJane Garside left Daisy Chainsaw in 1993.\n- Generationals are an American new wave duo formed in New Orleans, Louisiana.\n- Generationals consist of Ted Joyner and Grant Widmer.\n- Generationals released their debut album, \"Con Law\", in July 2009.\n- The woman referenced by \"Lullabies in a Glass Wilderness\" is the frontwoman of Queenadreena and Ruby Throat and is a former member of Daisy Chainsaw.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
